				(size 5.08 5.08)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "e54e08d4-570b-4481-ac3a-7ae6e7274d91")
	)
	(text "Todo list:\n\n[] - Replace 5v buck-regulator with newer type\n[] - Devise a protection circuit so that a high voltage on USB will not\n	kill the 5v buck-regulator (see lighting-controller-8M [2.0.0]\n	- 2 ideal-diodes to mux the 5v?\n	- ideal diode from Vbus to Vin?\n	- Comparator to detect when VBus > 5V?\n	- Turn off USB load-switch (input) whenever 5V regulator is active?\n		- Be careful of the load switch (output)! Don't want that turning on if\n		output is higher! Software can check, but is that trustworthy enough?\n	- [BEST OPTION] Replace the 5V buck regulator with a buck-boost regulator!\n		- e.g. TPS63070 (4sw, ~ $0.50)\n			- 4th switch means it can block reverse voltages!\n			- Also means it can operate with a much lower voltage - 2.0V\n				- 3-4V when accounting for the input bridge rectifier\n\n[] - Replace 0603 0.1uF with 0402 version (already on board)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 2.54 215.9 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "efacf57b-8de5-4680-9085-975b93a884a6")
	)
